what changed and why:
- M8.A2 closed `done` on a *reworded* done-when. The old clause 3
  ("`-M ze0` reproduces the ce_qemu_probe access list") was a board defect:
  a machine that maps sh4-ccn at 0xff000000 cannot emit the `-M none` list,
  and already differs with the same run.sh extents (1 vs 8, C-4312). The new
  clause is ze0-specific and falsifiable. The 0x38 store and the 0x5bd0
  tlb_miss moved to M8.A3 as loader follow-ups, not gates.
- the record defect I caught independently while the navigator reviewed: the
  EXP presented `final pc 0x00000000`, `pr`, `delayed_pc`, "2 854 passes" and
  `0xa801045e` as results. run.sh samples HMP on a wall-clock loop
  (run.sh:542-548). My 3x2 runs and the navigator's 6+10 runs gave different
  PCs every time and never produced 0xa801045e. Replaced with the stable
  observables + a repeat-run table; C-4311 rewritten to pin `--qemu` (PATH is
  11.1.3, where the probe returns 0 accesses).
- M8.A10 bumps the pin to 8.2.10, makes QEMU_PINS per-version (a full build
  refuses an unpinned tarball) and adds `--check-version V`, which probes a
  release in minutes without building. That is the precondition for M8.A9.
- M8.A9 (new) ports the *intent* of the five patches to 11.1.3, with the
  per-hunk recipe in docs/research/qemu-ze0-port-delta.md. Its Precheck
  carries both application columns because they disagree, and its Scope
  opens with the `mmaped` trap.

